## Example Audit

```markdown
### 1. Executive Verdict
**Verdict:** `NEEDS_WORK`  
**Summary:** Found 6 hardcoded hex colors, arbitrary pixel paddings that break dark mode theming, and an ad-hoc clickable `div` instead of the system `<Button>` primitive.

### 2. Design System Scorecard Matrix
| Dimension | Rating (1-5) | Status | Notes |
| :--- | :---: | :---: | :--- |
| **Token Adherence** | 2/5 | BLOCK | Raw hex `#3B82F6` and arbitrary `p-[13px]` bypass theme variables |
| **Component Reusability** | 2/5 | WARN | Reinvents button using `div onClick` without keyboard handlers |
| **Semantic HTML Standards** | 3/5 | WARN | Missing `<header>` and `<nav>` landmarks |
| **Styling Hygiene** | 4/5 | PASS | Clean flexbox layout with no `!important` flags |

### 3. Ranked Normalization Findings

#### [BLOCKER] Replace Custom Clickable Div with System Button
- **Location:** `src/components/UserProfileCard.tsx#L25-L31`
- **Violation Type:** Component Reinvention & Non-Tokenized Colors
- **Why It Matters:** Hardcoded `#3B82F6` ignores dark mode and theming; lacks built-in focus-visible rings and disabled states.
- **Token Alignment Diff:**
```diff
- <div 
-   onClick={handleFollow} 
-   className="bg-[#3B82F6] hover:bg-[#2563EB] text-white p-[13px] rounded-[7px] cursor-pointer text-center"
- >
-   Follow User
- </div>
+ <Button variant="primary" size="md" onClick={handleFollow}>
+   Follow User
+ </Button>
```

### 4. Dialectic System Inquiries
1. What design token represents our standard card corner radius: `rounded-md` or `rounded-lg`?
```
